In heterogeneous graph context representation (HGC), a word is portrayed as a concatenation embedding of its word ($W_e$), entity type ($W_t$), and co-reference embedding ($W_c$). This composite embedding is then input into a BiLSTM to convert the document $D$ into a vectorized form using the equation: BiLSTM([W$_e$:W$_t$:W$_c$]). Following the methodology of \cite{zeng-etal-2015-distant}, a heterogeneous graph is constructed based on sentence and mention nodes.
